WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV — ai-reads-human (90s) AI-synthesized studio narration

1
00:00:01.718 --> 00:00:08.556
Modern MCP and JSON-RPC agent stacks convert typed memory into UTF-8 text,

2
00:00:08.556 --> 00:00:12.159
BPE tokens, and AST dicts on every hop.

3
00:00:16.576 --> 00:00:21.559
By locking a 20,000-record corpus across 34 parsers and tokenizers,

4
00:00:21.559 --> 00:00:25.799
every layer of serialization overhead becomes measurable.

5
00:00:30.216 --> 00:00:35.095
This three-dimensional funnel contrasts sprawling JSON and YAML

6
00:00:35.095 --> 00:00:40.051
token clouds against compact 280-nanojoule fixed binary records.

7
00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:50.620
Even fast C libyaml burns 249 times more energy than binary structs,

8
00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:55.687
while BPE tokenization adds 27.7 microjoules per record.

9
00:01:00.104 --> 00:01:08.541
Executable specification tests expose real-world silent data corruption across loose text parsers alongside energy bloat.

10
00:01:12.957 --> 00:01:19.488
Dual-channel harnesses separate clean process L3 counters from noisy shared-host L2 windows,

11
00:01:19.488 --> 00:01:21.902
leaving measured_j honestly unset.
